        "Subsection 4.5.1 — Why Financial Execution Governs the Pace of Peace. Across post-conflict reconstruction, sovereign debt workouts, and natural-resource settlements, financial disbursement presents a persistent temporal paradox. Signatories arriving from years of mistrust demand immediate fiscal dividends to pay fighters, stabilise treasuries, and reward hesitant constituencies; simultaneously, guarantors and damaged communities recognise that money transferred upon ink alone vanishes long before permanent courts, municipal registries, or border commissions exist. Once capital has left external control upon signature, diplomatic leverage collapses to rhetorical protests whenever armed factions miss disarmament calendars or provincial ministries divert shared allocations.",
