            "This is analogous to bottleneck analysis in production systems, where throughput may be constrained by the first stage whose capacity is insufficient. The analogy is useful but limited. A social or political condition is not merely a machine capacity, and it would be inappropriate to reduce a community's concerns to friction in a production line. The analytical point is narrower: a sequential dependency can make the earliest unsatisfied condition decisive for the immediate release calculation.",
