            "Withholding a reserve does not make the underlying risk disappear. It allocates who bears a portion of the loss if a specified event occurs and changes when a portion of the pledge becomes available. A performance bond may strengthen incentives or provide a source of recovery, but its practical value depends on enforceability, custody, and the conditions for drawing it. A reserve that is inaccessible to the intended beneficiary or that can be released without review may provide little protection.",
