            "The schedule's sequence can be understood as a commitment device. Early release supplies some liquidity after an initial verification condition; later release is withheld until deeper institutional and generational conditions are established. The design seeks to make future benefits contingent on observable performance rather than relying solely on promises made at signature. Its credibility depends on whether the parties expect the conditions to be applied consistently and whether the custodian can resist unilateral pressure.",
