            "An audit begins by transcribing the inputs exactly as displayed: the four tranche shares, which sequential gates are satisfied, the applicable reserve settings, and the rupture reading that determines whether a freeze is active. The analyst then reproduces gross met tranches before applying the reserves. This order makes it possible to spot whether a disagreement concerns the milestone state, the reserve calculation, or the emergency rule.",
            "For the existing case with the first three gates satisfied, gross met value is 80 per cent. Under the default terms, the clawback retains 8 percentage points and the performance bond retains 5, so 67 per cent is releasable while Final Cession remains unmet. The unearned final share remains separate from those two reserves. A reader who reports only '33 per cent held' obscures the difference between reserved value and value still conditional on the last gate.",
