        {
          title: "Distributional effects, remedies, and the people behind the account",
          paragraphs: [
            "A release schedule distributes both resources and risk. The party that controls certification may influence when funds become available; the party that bears the cost of a delay may be a different institution or population altogether. A technically neutral percentage can therefore have unequal effects, especially where one side has greater fiscal capacity or where services depend on timely transfers. Analysis should identify who benefits, who bears the burden, and whose interests are represented in the oversight process.",
            "A conditional mechanism should not make essential services contingent on a condition that affected people cannot influence. If the purpose of the pledge is to support health, education, or reconstruction, withholding funds may harm intended beneficiaries rather than the officials whose conduct the condition seeks to change. The parties should examine whether the instrument needs protected humanitarian channels, direct beneficiary safeguards, or a more graduated response to non-compliance. Such provisions require legal negotiation; they should not be improvised as exceptions to the engine's declared rules.",
            "Remedies should be proportionate to the breach and connected to the purpose of the instrument. A freeze may preserve funds during an acute crisis, but a permanent freeze without review can transform a protective measure into an indefinite penalty. An agreement can define review dates, reinstatement conditions, and procedures for distinguishing deliberate obstruction from inability to perform. These are normative and legal choices beyond the mathematical freeze state represented in the platform.",
            "The agreement should also clarify how disputes affect amounts already released. A clawback may be available only under defined circumstances and due process; a performance bond may secure a specified obligation but not every possible loss. The fact that the model labels a reserve does not determine the trustee's legal power to transfer it or the beneficiary's right to claim it.",
            "Transparency must be balanced with privacy and safety. Financial data and certification records support accountability, while personal information, witness identities, or sensitive operational details may require protection. A good disclosure framework states what will be public, who can inspect restricted material, how records are retained, and what process applies to a disclosure challenge.",
            "The ultimate beneficiary of a peace-related fund is rarely just the signatory government. It may include displaced people, local communities, former combatants, public-service users, or claimants with distinct legal rights. A design that treats the account as a bargaining asset alone can miss those interests. Fiduciary analysis asks not only whether the money is conserved but whether its custody and use remain faithful to the purposes for which it was committed."
          ]
        },
        {
          title: "Using comparative scholarship without overstating causation",
          paragraphs: [
            "The technical literature on project finance and public-private partnerships explains how cash flows are prioritised, how reserve accounts support debt service, and how covenants can restrict distributions when performance weakens. Those concepts help students understand the mechanics of a waterfall, but a financial covenant in a commercial project does not carry the same public-law consequences as a sovereign peace agreement. The analogy should illuminate a mechanism, not erase the difference in parties and rights.",
            "The public-finance literature adds a different lens. IMF fiscal transparency standards ask whether fiscal risks, public assets, and commitments are comprehensively reported. OECD budget-governance principles emphasise a credible medium-term framework, transparent execution, and independent oversight. These standards help assess whether a restricted account remains visible to public institutions, but neither directly determines the legality or merits of an escrow.",
            "Historical evaluation requires a further distinction between mechanism and outcome. A project may fail despite an oversight account because of political pressure or weak administrative capacity; another may survive for reasons unrelated to its financial architecture. The existence of a reserve does not prove that the reserve caused compliance. Causal claims require evidence about the counterfactual, the sequence of events, and competing explanations.",
            "The Chad-Cameroon case is particularly valuable for this reason. The World Bank's Independent Evaluation Group examines the project's implementation and development objectives, while official statements document the suspension and subsequent exit. A scholarly account may interpret the political economy differently. A rigorous lecture separates those layers: primary sources establish the legal and administrative events; evaluation sources assess project performance; scholarship develops explanations.",
            "For the Algiers Accords and UNCC, primary documents should carry the account of the mandate, source of authority, and payment structure. Later institutional summaries help explain administration and closure, but should not substitute for the resolutions or declarations when making a legal claim. This is a general source hierarchy, not a claim that institutional reports are infallible.",
            "Students should mark each sentence in a case analysis as a fact, a legal interpretation, a causal inference, or a normative lesson. This simple annotation often reveals that a seemingly factual conclusion depends on a scholarly interpretation or on a premise not supported by the cited source. The goal is not to avoid interpretation but to make its basis visible."
          ]
        },
        {
          title: "Final account of the instrument's scope",
          paragraphs: [
            "The waterfall's formal proof concerns conservation, ordering, reserve treatment, and the release consequence of the inputs the engine receives. It does not create legal custody, verify the truth of a milestone, or decide who is entitled to a payment under an external agreement. Those questions require the governing text, an authorised custodian, and a process that can be reviewed by affected parties.",
            "Use the published result as an auditable state report: identify the amount released, the amount held by each defined category, the gate position, and the freeze status. Pair the arithmetic with evidence and authority, and keep scenario overrides separate from operational records. That is how exact accounting can support, rather than replace, fiduciary and public accountability."
          ]
        }
